  <data name="Home_Bridge_Only" xml:space="preserve"><value>The earbuds play through A2DP Bridge ({0}), but their controls are unreachable: the battery and earbud settings need A2DP Bridge 2.0.2 or later on a Classic connection.</value></data>
  <data name="Badge_Bridge_AudioOnly" xml:space="preserve"><value>Audio plays through A2DP Bridge's dedicated USB adapter ({0}). Windows cannot see that link.</value></data>
  <data name="Badge_Bridge_Windows" xml:space="preserve"><value>Audio plays through A2DP Bridge's dedicated USB adapter ({0}); the earbud settings are still controlled over Windows Bluetooth.</value></data>
  <data name="Badge_Bridge_Control" xml:space="preserve"><value>Audio plays through A2DP Bridge's dedicated USB adapter ({0}); EncoDeck reads the battery and changes earbud settings through A2DP Bridge too.</value></data>
  <data name="Bridge_Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>A2DP Bridge (dedicated USB Bluetooth adapter, experimental)</value></data>
  <data name="Bridge_Summary.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>A2DP Windows Bridge takes over a dedicated USB Bluetooth adapter and sends audio to your earbuds with its own Bluetooth stack in LDAC, LHDC V5, aptX HD and more, without test-signed drivers. EncoDeck downloads and starts it, and recognizes and controls earbuds connected through it on the home page.</value></data>
