  <data name="Bridge_UninstallTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Uninstall the A2DP Bridge component?</value></data>
  <data name="Bridge_UninstallBody" xml:space="preserve"><value>This quits the A2DPWB background process EncoDeck manages, deletes its files (about 25 MB) and removes startup entries that point to it. A2DPWB's settings folder (pairings, firmware, logs) is kept; an A2DP Windows Bridge you installed yourself is not affected.</value></data>
  <data name="Bridge_UninstallRestore" xml:space="preserve"><value>Also give the {0} adapter(s) A2DPWB took back to Windows (recommended; one administrator prompt)</value></data>
