  <data name="LeAudio_ConfirmTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Change how the earbuds connect?</value></data>
  <data name="LeAudio_ConfirmSwitch" xml:space="preserve"><value>EncoDeck first turns multipoint off and confirms the setting, so a phone cannot take over the connection. The earbuds will no longer connect to two devices simultaneously. If confirmation fails, the switch stops.

When asked, put the earbuds in the case, open the lid and hold the case button to enter pairing mode. Once pairing mode is detected, EncoDeck removes this PC's old pairing with the earbuds (pairing records on your phone and other devices are kept) and pairs both earbuds over LE Audio automatically; audio stops meanwhile.

Afterwards Windows lists two entries with the same name (one is the other earbud), and audio plays through "Speakers (earbud name)".</value></data>
  <data name="LeAudio_ConfirmRestore" xml:space="preserve"><value>EncoDeck will remove this PC's LE Audio and associated Classic Bluetooth pairings; audio will stop. After cleanup, put the earbuds in pairing mode and manually pair them using Add device in Windows Bluetooth settings.</value></data>
