  <data name="LeAudio_Disclaimer.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Experimental: so far verified only on the OPPO Enco X4. Over LE Audio, spatial audio, Hi-Res and dual-device connection may be unavailable.</value></data>
  <data name="LeAudio_Help.Header" xml:space="preserve"><value>About LE Audio</value></data>
  <data name="LeAudio_Guide.Content" xml:space="preserve"><value>Read the guide and how it works</value></data>
  <data name="LeAudio_HelpRequirements.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Requires Windows 11 24H2 or later and a Bluetooth adapter and driver with LE Audio support (for example Intel "Smart Sound Technology for Bluetooth LE Audio"). Turning on "Use LE Audio when available" in Settings → Bluetooth &amp; devices → Devices is recommended.</value></data>
  <data name="LeAudio_HelpSwitch.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>These earbuds do not appear as an LE device in Windows' "Add device", so pairing there uses Classic Bluetooth. EncoDeck pairs their LE address directly, and Windows generates an associated Classic pairing record. Over LE Audio, EncoDeck uses GATT control only. The other earbud's address is read from the first earbud's advertisement. No setting on the earbuds is changed.</value></data>
  <data name="LeAudio_HelpLimits.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Afterwards the other earbud is listed separately in Bluetooth settings under the same name. Over LE Audio, EncoDeck controls the earbuds over GATT, so noise control, battery and the other features keep working. Known issue: when playback starts, one earbud is occasionally about 7.5 ms behind the other, pulling the sound to one side; stop all audio for a few seconds and play again to realign.</value></data>
  <data name="LeAudio_HelpRestore.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>To return to Classic Bluetooth, click Restore Classic Bluetooth to remove this PC's earbud pairings. After cleanup, put the earbuds in pairing mode and manually pair them using Add device in Windows Bluetooth settings. EncoDeck does not pair them over Classic Bluetooth automatically.</value></data>
